QuestGuidance.Register("en",85,{
[2689]="7004E74B\n1\tClear the entrance to the Spider Tunnels\tClear the entrance to the Spider Tunnels.\n2\tSecure the path leading to Etterfang\tSecure the path leading to Etterfang.\n3\tFind and defeat Etterfang Foulmaw\tFind and defeat Etterfang Foulmaw.\n",
[2690]="7004E74D\n1\tClear the entrance to the Spider Tunnels\tClear the entrance to the Spider Tunnels.\n2\tSecure the path leading to Etterfang\tSecure the path leading to Etterfang.\n3\tFind and defeat Etterfang Foulmaw\tFind and defeat Etterfang Foulmaw.\n",
[2691]="7000D4E3\n1\tCollect Angmarim staves (total: 5)\tThe priests and priestesses of Angmar can be found near the altars throughout the Bails of Himbar, which lie to the west of Gath Forthnír. Maerchiniath has instructed you to go forth and defeat the priests of Angmar, bringing him their staves as evidence of your success.\n2\tBring staves back to Maerchiniath in Gath Forthnír\tGath Forthnír is to the east of Himbar. You should return to Maerchiniath with the staves you took from the priests of Angmar.\n",
[2692]="7000D6B5\n1\tDefeat Gaunt-men in Imlad Balchorth (total: 5)\tGaunt-men can be found in western Imlad Balchorth, west of Myrkworth. Sigar has asked you to destroy the Gaunt-men in Imlad Balchorth.\n2\tTalk to Sigar\tSigar is at Myrkworth, east of Imlad Balchorth. Having killed the Gaunt-men as asked, return to Sigar in Myrkworth and tell him the deed is done.\n",
[2693]="7001570D\n1\tTalk to Gúthi\tGúthi can be found at the Cross-roads of Ash in the western Flaming Deeps. You should speak with Gúthi when you are ready to travel to the ancient forge of Hurmulkezer.\n2\tTalk to Gúthi at the Cross-roads of Ash\tGúthi is at the Cross-roads of Ash in the western Flaming Deeps. Gúthi will be pleased to hear Dolpan was unable to finish crafting his weapon at the ancient forge.\n",
[2694]="70035669\n1\tTravel to the Hedge Maze in the Bree-land Horsefields\tIn celebration of springtime, the residents of Bree-land have built an impressive Hedge Maze. Folks are travelling from all around to try their hand at navigating the maze, drink, and make merriment. Travel to the Horsefields in Bree-land to join in the festivities. Welcome to the Spring Festival!\n2\tTravel to the Hedge Maze in Bree-land to participate in the Spring celebration\tEach year all of Middle-earth celebrates the end of winter with a merry Spring Festival. Head to the Hedge Maze, put on by the men of Bree-land, to begin joining in the festivities!\n",
[2695]="70071E90\n1\tReach Esteemed standing with the Hamât Renewed\tAs Hamât rises anew, you have proven an invaluable ally. Mizâdi and her agents look to you for further assistance. You should return to Mizâdi's encampment and treat with Lumgâna.\n2\tSpeak to Lumgâna at Mizâdi's encampment\tAs Hamât rises anew, you have proven an invaluable ally. Mizâdi and her agents look to you for further assistance. You should return to Mizâdi's encampment and treat with Lumgâna.\n",
[2696]="70072AFF\n1\tSpeak with Dabâr at Ahâba\tDabâr warns that his tale is one of caution and offers it as reward for rescuing him, and the other from the gaol. Speak with him near the bridge in the north of Ahâba.\n2\tSpeak with Dabâr in Ahâba\tDabâr paused. You should ask him to continue his tale. You can find him near the bridge on the northern side of Ahâba.\n3\tSpeak with Dabâr to hear the remainder of his story\tDabâr paused again, conscious of the eyes upon him. He beckoned you closer to finish his tale. You should speak with him near the bridge on the north side of Ahâba.\n",
[2697]="70072B00\n1\tSpeak with Malgâras at Ahâba\tMalgâras bids you stay and listen to him. Speak with him beneath the canopy east of the stable-master in Ahâba.\n2\tSpeak with Malgâras\tMalgâras appears finished, a smile spreading on his face. Speak with him again beneath the canopy near the stable-master in Ahâba.\n",
[2698]="70072AFE\n1\tSpeak with Vilgêra at Ahâba\tVilgêra wishes to share a tale as a reward for helping to release him. Speak with him beneath the canopy near the sheep pen in Ahâba.\n2\tSpeak with Vilgêras in Ahâba\tVilgêras stops, his voice growing hoarse. He asked you to step closer to hear the remainder of the tale. He awaits you near the sheep pen in Ahâba.\n",
[2699]="700375B8\n1\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild\tReeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. Thane Ordlac asked if you would broach the subject of a feast in celebration of the victory at Bardh-dorám with Reeve Fríthild.\n2\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild to join the feast\tReeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. You should speak with Reeve Fríthild to join the feast.\n3\tTalk to Thane Ordlac\tThane Ordlac is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. You should speak with Thane Ordlac regarding the treachery at the feast.\n",
[2700]="70028C94\n1\tOpen cages (total: 3)\tPrison-cages may be found within Brôntrig, east of the tower where Answith is hiding. Answith has asked you to enter Brôntrig and free any prisoners you find there.\n2\tTalk to Answith in the Isendale\tAnswith is encamped at the tower, west of Brôntrig. You should return to Answith with news of your success.\n",
[2701]="70066063\n1\tPick up the crate of tonics\tEliaril has asked you to bring a crate of tonics to the Calembel barracks. The crate is in a small hamlet, outside of the city.\n2\tBring the crate to Maeron\tEliaril has asked you to bring a crate of tonics to Maeron. Maeron is in the Calembel barracks.\n3\tMaeron has asked you to distribute tonics to wounded soldiers in the Calembel barracks.\t\n4\tReturn to Maeron\tYou should let Maeron know that have brought healing potions to many of the wounded soldiers in the barracks. Maeron is in the Calembel barracks.\n",
[2702]="700698B8\n1\tSpeak to Ransroth\tTalk to Ransroth.\n",
