[2706]="7000ACE0\n1\tPresent your Ceremonial Blades to Cannasgam at Tinnudir\030Craft Ceremonial Blades (total: 5)\tCannasgam is at Tinnudir in Evendim. Cannasgam has asked you to forge the ceremonial blades, which the Rangers of the North confer upon their greatest heroes.\n",
[2707]="7000ACDE\n1\tPresent your Ceremonial Daggers to Cannasgam at Tinnudir\030Craft Ceremonial Daggers (total: 5)\tCannasgam is at Tinnudir in Evendim. Cannasgam has asked you to forge ceremonial daggers and bring them to her.\n",
[2708]="7001ECCF\n1\tIssue your challenge to join the battle\tThe stone may be found outside Fennas Guldur, east of Thangúlhad. Rodelleth has bidden you issue a challenge at the stone before the gates of Fennas Guldur and defeat the forces of Dol Guldur which answer.\n2\tTalk to Rodelleth at Thangúlhad\tRodelleth is at Thangúlhad, west of Fennas Guldur. With the aid of your companions, you have defeated the Gloom of Nurn before the gates of Fennas Guldur and struck a mighty blow against the power of Dol Guldur. You should now return to Rodelleth with the tale of your victory.\n",
[2709]="7001757E\n1\tDefeat Nightshine\tDefeat the World Eater in the Dark Delvings\n2\tReturn to Dithrik in the Foundations of Stone\t\n",
[2710]="7004BD2F\n1\tConfront Sagróg, the Bitter Warden\tIn the darkness of the Abyss of Mordath, it is the Bitter Warden who protects the most well-concealed secrets of the Dark Lord, but his identity has ever been a mystery to both the slaves and guards of the Mordath.\n2\tDefeat Sagróg, the Bitter Warden after fully healing the Unseen Spear and forcing his surrender within 10 seconds\tYou and your fellows must defeat Sagróg, the Bitter Warden after fully healing the Unseen Spear. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2711]="7002BD16\n1\tFind the Ring of Acid within the depths of Isengard\tYou must find the bearer of the Ring of Acid.\n2\tDefeat Iorweth\tYou must defeat Iorweth, bearer of the Ring of Acid. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2712]="7003332C\n1\tDefeat the Easterlings in the clearing\tThe people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...\n2\tShatter the Easterling Army\tThe people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind... This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefend the clearing from the Easterling assault\tThe people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...\n",
[2713]="70022483\n1\tReach Balhest\tBalhest is in the throne room of Ost Elendil.\n2\tDefeat Balhest\tBalhest must be defeated while his sorceresses watch his demise. Balhest has great love for his sorceresses, and if he sees them all suitably weakened, he will intervene to save them. When he does, show them how weak their master is. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat the High Sorceresses (total: 3)\tWith Balhest defeated and their minds reeling, defeat the High Sorceresses and end their misery.\n",
[2714]="7001EEF8\n1\tLight the Challenger's Brazier, then engage and defeat all three champions at once\tThe Sword-hall is at Dol Guldur, the enemy stronghold of Mirkwood. You should endeavour to defeat all three champions of the Sword-hall at once -- a great challenge that will earn you much renown.\n",
[2715]="7001E685\n1\tDefeat the Caeryg in the southern room\030Defeat the Caeryg in the western room\tDeep in the Water-works, there are great Caeryg lurking. You should find them in the hidden rooms of the Water-works and banish them from Moria.\n2\tDefeat Caerlûg\tIn the farthest depths of the Water-works, there is the greatest of Caeryg, Caerlug. Defeat him to claim your reward.\n",
[2716]="700459BE\n1\tConfront the High-sorcerer of Harad and the Woe of Khand\tOn the Pelennor Fields, two of the Nazgûl stand guard outside the Causeway Forts. If their vile assault is to be ended completely, they must be banished together at once.\n2\tDefeat the High-sorcerer of Harad and the Woe of Khand within 10 seconds of the other's defeat\tOn the Pelennor Fields, two of the Nazgûl stand guard outside the Causeway Forts. If their vile assault is to be ended completely, they must be banished together at once. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2717]="700223A1\n1\tCall forth Chieftain Gûrsh\tChieftain Gûrsh is very fond of his craban-warders. To shatter the confidence of the invaders, defeat Gûrsh and all his Dark-wing Warders together. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tDefeat Chieftain Gûrsh\tChieftain Gûrsh is very fond of his craban-warders. To shatter the confidence of the invaders, defeat Gûrsh and all his Dark-wing Warders together. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat the Dark-wing warders (total: 16)\tDefeat the Dark-wing warders.\n",
[2718]="7002ADBF\n1\tFind the bearer of the Ring of Lightning\tYou must find the bearer of the Ring of Lightning.\n2\tDefeat Kâlbak\tNo crystals may be shattered while defeating Kâlbak. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2719]="7002497E\n1\tReach Ivar\tIvar is waiting deep within Ost Dunhoth.\n2\tDefeat Ivar and his Champions\tIvar's champions draw power from dark corruptions. To show the Gaunt-lord that you fear no evil power, defeat Ivar and his champions without removing any corruptions. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2720]="7002B09B\n1\tFind the bearer of the ring of Shadow\tYou must find the bearer of the Ring of Shadow.\n2\tDefeat Bukot\tThe Orc must be defeated before shadow consumes the greater part of the Throne-room. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
})
